<statement>
<p>Suppose enrollment in a class was 59 in the fall and 65 in the following spring.</p>
<p>It was a <fillin characters="20"/> percent </p>
<p><ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha"><li>decrease</li> 
<li>increase</li> 
</ol></p>



</statement>
<answer>
<p><ul><li>10</li><li>B: increase</li></ul></p>
</answer>
<solution><p>Because 65 is bigger than 59 it is a percent increase.</p>
<p>The percent increase is <m>\displaystyle{100}{\left(\frac{{{65}-{59}}}{{59}}\right)}={100}\cdot\frac{{6}}{{59}}\approx{10}\%</m>.</p></solution>
</myopenmath>